Aerie-Purpose: Put the "Ctrl+Tab cycles recent tabs" switch in the Sidebar section of Settings, let the settings page write its pref, and give the page its strings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private (prefs_util.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #269. The row, settings-aerie-recent-tabs-row, is a Lit element in the overlay
(chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/aerie_recent_tabs_row.*). It is a
settings-toggle-button on the pref aerie.sidebar.recent_tab_switcher (a boolean, registered by
components/aerie_sidebar/aerie_sidebar_prefs.cc, on by default). When the switch is off, Ctrl+Tab goes
along the tab order as Chromium does, and no card overlay shows. The pref name is a string literal in
the settings_private allowlist, as for the other Aerie prefs, and a test compares it with
aerie_sidebar::kRecentTabSwitcherPref. Its strings are in the overlay's aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp, which
patches/sidebar/0022 includes in generated_resources.grd; this patch hands them to the page. The element
sits in the "Sidebar" section, under the "Links open" row of patches/sidebar/0053.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
@@ -502,6 +502,11 @@
   // Aerie: how a link that would open a new tab opens (issue #141). The name is
   // aerie_tab_model::kLinksOpen; a test compares the two.
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.links_open"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
+  // Aerie: whether Ctrl+Tab cycles the recent tabs with a card overlay (issue
+  // #269). The name is aerie_sidebar::kRecentTabSwitcherPref; a test compares
+  // the two.
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.sidebar.recent_tab_switcher"] =
+      settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
   // Aerie: the global switch of the rules of auto-filing folders (issue #139).
   // The name is aerie_tab_model::kFolderRulesEnabled; a test compares the two.
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.folders.rules_enabled"] =
